findings.remediation:
Enable IAM database authentication on the RDS instance so access is granted
via IAM instead of static passwords:
resource "aws_db_instance" "this" {
  # ...
  iam_database_authentication_enabled = true
}

Copy resource tags to automated snapshots so they inherit ownership and
cost-allocation metadata:
resource "aws_db_instance" "this" {
  # ...
  copy_tags_to_snapshot = true
}

Attach a permissions boundary to the IAM role so its effective permissions
can never exceed the boundary policy, even if broader policies are attached later:
resource "aws_iam_role" "this" {
  # ...
  permissions_boundary = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/YourBoundaryPolicy"
}

Add a description to the IAM role documenting its purpose and owner:
resource "aws_iam_role" "this" {
  # ...
  description = "Application role for <workload>; owner: <team>"
}
